212|The singer's [[repertoire]] was [[pious]], but his [[narcissistic]] and [[intransigent]] manager gave a [[backhanded]] compliment to the press.
213|The critic chose to [[eschew]] a [[plausible]] but [[ungainly]] theory that could [[engender]] debate; no [[substitute]] was offered.
214|The team agreed to [[delve]] deeper; the firm wished to [[consolidate]] its power and [[moderate]] its tone, but it would [[spurn]] a [[redundant]] rule.
215|Her [[panache]] won the room; she would [[verify]] each claim, since a [[flaccid]] case could [[satirize]] itself, and an [[ascetic]] monk agreed.
216|The [[unassailable]] ruler faced a [[disaffected]] clerk in [[abject]] misery, who would [[withhold]] his vote or [[defer]] it.
217|The court did not [[delineate]] its rule; her [[acumen]] was clear, for the [[virulent]] attack could only [[spur]] the [[phlegmatic]] board to act.
218|The rival chose to [[sabotage]] the plan and [[aggrieve]] the staff; the [[arduous]] climb left the [[venal]] guide [[gloomy]].
219|The storm would [[deject]] the group, and the cost would [[curtail]] the trip; his [[persistence]] was admired, though the [[feckless]] clerk made the files [[elude]] him.
